To find out how many pages they have finished reading in total, we need to first calculate the number of pages each person can read in 240 minutes.

Rene can read 30 pages in 60 minutes, so in 240 minutes, he can read:
\( \frac{240}{60} \times 30 = 4 \times 30 = 120 \) pages.

Lulu can read 27 pages in 60 minutes, so in 240 minutes, she can read:
\( \frac{240}{60} \times 27 = 4 \times 27 = 108 \) pages.

Cherry can read 25 pages in 60 minutes, so in 240 minutes, she can read:
\( \frac{240}{60} \times 25 = 4 \times 25 = 100 \) pages.

Now, to find the total number of pages they have read, we add the pages each person has read:
\( 120 + 108 + 100 = 328 \) pages.

 
